    "final_cot": "Image description: The figure is a circle, with two chords intersecting inside the circle. The circumference is divided into four arcs, labeled respectively as 3a° at the top, 6a° on the right, 4a° at the lower left, and 5a° on the left. The two chords intersect inside the circle, and the interior angle on the right is labeled 6. Reasoning: The four arcs form the whole circle, so 3a + 6a + 4a + 5a = 360, that is, 18a = 360, giving a = 20. The angle formed by two chords intersecting inside a circle equals half the sum of the two intercepted opposite arcs. Angle 6 corresponds to the right arc 6a° and the opposite left arc 5a°, so angle 6 = (6a + 5a) / 2 = 11a / 2. Substituting a = 20, angle 6 = 110°.",
